B5 backfill fix — prepared 2026-10-22, NOT applied. Hasan's call after part A of
docs/studio/end-to-end/B5/HASAN-STEP.md (W1-W8).

What: `withSpokenSpans` (src/features/studio/services/transcript-doc.ts) gives a word
stamped < 50 ms the silence before it (up to 1 s). It was written for whisper.cpp, which
stamps some real words 0-20 ms long at the next word's start. AssemblyAI times every word
in ms and its short words are measured ("a" 16 ms, "I" 32-48 ms). On M2 (nine clips, 1,820
AssemblyAI words) HEAD moves 76 starts earlier, 25 of them by >= 0.5 s. A duration rule
cannot tell the two apart (whisper's "the" is 20 ms, AssemblyAI's "a" 16 ms; a <= 20 ms
rule still moves 28 of the 76, up to 708 ms), so the backfill now goes by the transcript's
engine: whisper (or no engine recorded) keeps it; AssemblyAI and ElevenLabs words stay as
delivered. On M2: 76 of 76 moved words keep their own start (0 moved).

Apply (repo root, clean tree):
  git apply docs/studio/end-to-end/B5/backfill-fix.patch
  npx vitest run src/features/studio/services/transcript-doc.test.ts src/features/studio/services/text-delete.test.ts
  npm run check:types
  git add src/features/studio/services/transcript-doc.ts src/features/studio/services/transcript-doc.test.ts src/features/studio/hooks/useTextEdit.ts
  git commit -m "fix(studio): Transcript tab keeps AssemblyAI and ElevenLabs word starts (backfill whisper only)"

